.TH LIBNETPIPE 3 "June 2026" "netpipe v0.1.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
libnetpipe \- high-performance network stream-processing library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <netpipe.h>
.PP
.BI "np_err_t np_init(void);"
.br
.BI "void np_cleanup(void);"
.br
.BI "const char *np_strerror(np_err_t " err ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B libnetpipe
is a C11 library for high-performance, pipeline-driven network packet processing. It allows building complex capture, filtering, processing, and routing applications.
.PP
The execution model is based on a pipeline
.RB ( np_pipeline_t )
that feeds packets
.RB ( np_packet_t )
from one or more sources through optional filters and processors into one or more sinks.
.PP
Before calling any other library functions, the library must be initialized by calling
.BR np_init ().
When the application is done using the library, resources should be cleaned up by calling
.BR np_cleanup ().
.SH RETURN VALUES
Most functions in
.B libnetpipe
return a status code of type
.BR np_err_t .
The following error codes are defined:
.TP
.B NP_OK
Success (0).
.TP
.B NP_ERR_GENERIC
Generic/unspecified error (\-1).
.TP
.B NP_ERR_NOMEM
Out of memory (\-2).
.TP
.B NP_ERR_IO
Input/output error (\-3).
.TP
.B NP_ERR_PROTO
Protocol parsing or validation error (\-4).
.TP
.B NP_ERR_FILTER
Invalid filter expression or execution error (\-5).
.TP
.B NP_ERR_TIMEOUT
Operation timed out (\-6).
.TP
.B NP_ERR_NODEV
Device or file not found (\-7).
.TP
.B NP_ERR_PERM
Permission denied (\-8).
.TP
.B NP_ERR_EOF
End of file reached (\-9).
.PP
The function
.BR np_strerror ()
converts an
.B np_err_t
error code into a human-readable English string.
.SH EXAMPLE
The following is a minimal example that captures traffic from interface "eth0", filters for HTTP (port 80), and dumps it as a PCAP file:
.PP
.nf
#include <netpipe.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int main(void) {
    /* Initialize the library */
    if (np_init() != NP_OK) {
        fprintf(stderr, "Failed to initialize netpipe\\n");
        return 1;
    }

    /* Create a new pipeline context */
    np_pipeline_t *pl = np_pipeline_new();
    if (!pl) {
        fprintf(stderr, "Failed to create pipeline\\n");
        np_cleanup();
        return 1;
    }

    /* Add a live packet source */
    np_source_t *src = np_source_live("eth0", 65535, 1, 1000);
    np_pipeline_add_source(pl, src);

    /* Filter for port 80 */
    np_filter_t *flt = np_filter_port(80);
    np_pipeline_add_filter(pl, flt);

    /* Write filtered packets to a pcap file */
    np_sink_t *snk = np_sink_pcap("http_traffic.pcap");
    np_pipeline_add_sink(pl, snk);

    /* Run the pipeline (blocks until stopped or interrupted) */
    printf("Running netpipe pipeline... Press Ctrl-C to stop.\\n");
    np_err_t err = np_pipeline_run(pl);
    if (err != NP_OK) {
        fprintf(stderr, "Pipeline error: %s\\n", np_strerror(err));
    }

    /* Clean up resources */
    np_pipeline_free(pl);
    np_cleanup();
    return 0;
}
.fi
.SH COMPILING
To compile applications using
.BR libnetpipe ,
link against the static library and its dependencies:
.PP
.RS
.B gcc myapp.c -I/usr/local/include -L/usr/local/lib -lnetpipe -lpcap -lpthread -ldl -lm -o myapp
.RE
